# =============================================================================
# labwc environment — variables for everything the window manager starts
# =============================================================================
# This file is NOT a shell script. labwc parses it itself, one NAME=value per
# line, so that the values can be reloaded when labwc is reconfigured. A line
# starting with '#' is a comment; trailing comments are not supported.
#
# It is nearly empty on purpose. Everything that matters — XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP,
# XDG_SESSION_TYPE, QS_CONFIG_PATH, QT_QPA_PLATFORM, AQ_LOG — is already set by
# /usr/bin/aquarius-session before labwc is ever started, and labwc inherits it.
# Setting the same variable in two places is how they end up disagreeing.
#
# The three things worth knowing:
#
#   * XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP. labwc sets this to "labwc:wlroots" by default, but
#     ONLY if it is not already set. /usr/bin/aquarius-session sets it first, to
#     "Aquarius:wlroots", and that is deliberate: it is the name
#     xdg-desktop-portal uses to find our portal configuration. Do not override
#     it here — you would break screen recording without any warning.
#
#   * GDK_BACKEND. Never set it. It breaks the screencast portal.
#
#   * WLR_RENDERER. Setting this to "vulkan" switches labwc to the Vulkan
#     renderer, which is what HDR output will eventually need. It is NOT on by
#     default because it has not been tested on the NVIDIA driver on the bench.
#     When it is, this is the line that turns it on for everybody.
#
# This file is part of the read-only operating system. To change something for
# yourself, copy this whole folder to ~/.config/labwc/ and edit that copy —
# labwc reads your own folder before this one.
# =============================================================================

# Cursor theme and size, if the defaults are not what you want:
# XCURSOR_THEME=Adwaita
# XCURSOR_SIZE=24

# Keyboard layout, if the system setting is not what you want:
# XKB_DEFAULT_LAYOUT=se
